Now, the tables can hold 5 people each. So, the next step is to figure out how many tables are needed to seat 40 people, with each table holding 5. To do this, I think I need to divide the number of people by the number of people per table. So that would be 40 divided by 5. Let me compute that: 40 ÷ 5 equals 8. So, 8 tables.

