Next, we need to determine how many shelves Mike will need. Each shelf can hold 9 books. To find the number of shelves needed, we can divide the number of books Mike has to put away by the number of books per shelf. However, since we can't have a fraction of a shelf, we need to round up to the nearest whole number if there's any remainder.

So, first, calculate the number of books Mike has to put away: 82 - 10 = 72.

Then, divide that number by the number of books per shelf: 72 / 9 = 8.

Since 72 is exactly divisible by 9, we don't need to round up. Therefore, Mike will need 8 shelves.
