The problem states that Nancy's class is going on a field trip to the zoo with 12 students and 3 adults. Each van can hold 5 people. To determine how many vans are needed, we first calculate the total number of people going on the trip.

$$
\text{Total people} = 12 \text{ students} + 3 \text{ adults} = 15 \text{ people}
