The problem involves determining how many people would be on each volleyball team if 23 managers and 7 employees split into 6 teams. The first step is to calculate the total number of people:

$$
23 \text{ managers} + 7 \text{ employees} = 30 \text{ people}
$$

Next, divide this total by the number of teams:

$$
30 \div 6 = 5
$$

Thus, each team would have 5 people. The final answer is:

$$
\boxed{5}
