Each worksheet has 7 problems, so the total number of problems across all worksheets is:  
$$
17 \text{ worksheets} \times 7 \text{ problems per worksheet} = 119 \text{ problems}
$$

**Step 2: Number of problems already graded**  
She has graded 8 worksheets, so the number of problems already graded is:  
$$
8 \text{ worksheets} \times 7 \text{ problems per worksheet} = 56 \text{ problems}
$$

**Step 3: Number of problems remaining**  
To find the number of problems left to grade, subtract the graded problems from the total:  
$$
119 \text{ problems} - 56 \text{ problems} = 63 \text{ problems}
$$

