$$
8 \times 7 = 56
$$

To find the number of problems remaining to be graded, subtract the number of graded problems from the total number of problems:

$$
119 - 56 = 63
$$

Alternatively, the number of ungraded worksheets is:

$$
17 - 8 = 9
$$

Each of these 9 worksheets has 7 problems, so the number of remaining problems is:

$$
9 \times 7 = 63
$$

Thus, the teacher has to grade $\boxed{63}$ more problems. 

