Total students = 65
Students not picked = 17
Students picked = 65 - 17

So 65 minus 17. Let me do that calculation. 65 minus 10 is 55, then minus 7 more would be 48. So 48 students were picked. 

Now, these 48 students are divided into 8 groups. The question is asking how many students are in each group. So, I need to divide the number of students by the number of groups. That would be 48 divided by 8. 

Let me do that division. 8 times 6 is 48, so 48 divided by 8 is 6. So each group would have 6 students. 

