Let me see, there's a problem here about Katie and her files. She started with 85 files on her computer. Then she deleted 40 of them. So first, I need to figure out how many files she had left after deleting those 40. 

So, if she had 85 and deleted 40, that would be 85 minus 40. Let me calculate that. 85 minus 40 is 45. Okay, so she has 45 files remaining. 

Now, the problem says she put the rest into folders, with 5 files in each one. So I need to figure out how many folders she needs. That would be taking the 45 files and dividing them by 5, right? Because each folder holds 5 files. 

